### Findings resolved within this candidate
RC-01: the original wrong-target page probe now refuses with exit 2. Destination
is derived from source page/pass/kind, rather than accepting an equal basename.
RC-02: the original unrelated return-line probe now refuses with exit 2. NN and
subject are computed from source identity; typed origin is checked too. The suite
covers wrong same-NN subject and verifies target/support remain unchanged.
RC-03: review-task-binding/2 explicitly includes normalized source book/page/pass
and assignment logical path. Equal task bytes at different source addresses bind
differently. Nonzero N7NN rendering works; nonzero N5NN address/binding derives
the correct N1NN identity. Original binding records are not rewritten.
The readable full review retains supplied judgment and surrounding-byte protection.
Rendering versus changed task/evidence/receipt/agreement checks pass the suite.

### Explicit compatibility limit
The pinned prime_review.py still accepts only 01NN capture identities. Consequently
the nonzero N5NN address can bind correctly but rendering refuses bad member at
that dependency. This is an observed supported-interface boundary, not full
nonzero workflow support. It was correctly reported rather than bypassing a pin.
Accept the constructor for bounded current 0-space use and its lab evidence;
do not claim general N-space production integration complete. A later reviewed
dependency/caller update must add nonzero identities before that route is usable.
prime_cycle's live whole-page binding is also unchanged; no live app wiring exists.
Supplied byte hashes do not authenticate custody; the constructor states that limit.

